\if{html}{\out{<a id="method-sql_server-order_object_fields"></a>}}
\if{latex}{\out{\hypertarget{method-sql_server-order_object_fields}{}}}
\subsection{Method \code{order_object_fields()}}{
SQL returns error "Invalid Descriptor Index" when reading in data that
contains fields with data types varbinary(max), varchar(max) or geometry
if these fields are not at the end of the SELECT statement. This is
annoying when reading in all fields. This function takes the names of all
the fields in a table/view, orders them by data type and returns an output
that can be used within a SQL query to avoid this issue.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#stable}{\figure{lifecycle-stable.svg}{options: alt='[Stable]'}}}{\strong{[Stable]}}
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{sql_server$order_object_fields(
  database = self$database,
  object,
  close_conn = TRUE
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{database}}{database with tables/views to fields from. Quoted
string, defaults to database used to create class.}

\item{\code{object}}{name of view/table, must not include the schema name;
quoted string, no default.}

\item{\code{close_conn}}{set whether to close the connection after query is run.
Generally this should be TRUE, only leave open if specific reason to do so,
such as using temporary tables. Logical, default TRUE.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
}
\if{html}{\out{<hr>}}
\if{html}{\out{<a id="method-sql_server-object_fields"></a>}}
\if{latex}{\out{\hypertarget{method-sql_server-object_fields}{}}}
\subsection{Method \code{object_fields()}}{
List of fields in an object (i.e. table/field).

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#stable}{\figure{lifecycle-stable.svg}{options: alt='[Stable]'}}}{\strong{[Stable]}}
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{sql_server$object_fields(
  database = self$database,
  catalog = self$catalog,
  schema = self$schema,
  objects = NULL,
  close_conn = TRUE
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{database}}{database with tables/views to fields from. Quoted
string, defaults to database used to create class.}

\item{\code{catalog}}{The name of the catalog the schema is in. Note that this
is only required when connecting to databricks. Quoted string, default
value from class when initiated.}

\item{\code{schema}}{The name of the schema. Note that this is only required when
connecting to databricks. Quoted string, default value from class when
initiated.}

\item{\code{objects}}{vector with table(s) and/or view(s) to get fields from.
Quoted string, default NULL includes all the tables & views in the database
(that have permissions to).}

\item{\code{close_conn}}{set whether to close the connection after query is run.
Generally this should be TRUE, only leave open if specific reason to do so,
such as using temporary tables. Logical, default TRUE.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
}
\if{html}{\out{<hr>}}
\if{html}{\out{<a id="method-sql_server-meta_data"></a>}}
\if{latex}{\out{\hypertarget{method-sql_server-meta_data}{}}}
\subsection{Method \code{meta_data()}}{
Create meta data from specified objects Defaults to all the objects
in the given databases, otherwise specify a list of specific objects to
create data for.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

Important: this function will fail if there are views & tables in the
database with the same name.
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{sql_server$meta_data(
  database = self$database,
  objects = NULL,
  details = FALSE,
  row_limit = NULL,
  date_filter = NULL,
  date_field = NULL,
  close_conn = TRUE
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{database}}{database with tables/views to create meta data for. Quoted
string, defaults to database used to create class.}

\item{\code{objects}}{vector with table(s) and/or view(s) to create meta data for.
Quoted string, defaults to all the tables & views in the database (that have
permissions to).}

\item{\code{details}}{indicate if want detailed output, adds fields showing
\% completion of data, number of unique values, proportion of completed
values are unique, date of the last non NULL value (where date is taken
from field provided by argument \code{date_field} or the first date/datetime
field in the object when \code{date_field} is NULL) and number of rows.
Note, depending on the size of the data, this can add significant
processing time. Consider use of \code{row_limit}, \code{date_filter} and
\code{date_field} to clauclate details on subset of data. Logical,
default FALSE.}

\item{\code{row_limit}}{limit the number of rows used to calculate the extra
details from. Integer; default 500000L.}

\item{\code{date_filter}}{set date to filter data by when when calculating the
extra details, useful where tables contain a large amount of data. Function
will apply as date_field >= date_filter. Quoted string, default NULL.}

\item{\code{date_field}}{set date field to filter & order data by when when
calculating the extra details, useful where tables contain a large amount
of data. Function will apply as date_field >= date_filter. Order will have
affect when number of rows returned is greater than set via row_limit, i.e.
the most recent row_limit number of records will be used, according to the
date_field field. Quoted string, default NULL.}

\item{\code{close_conn}}{set whether to close the connection after query is run.
Generally this should be TRUE, only leave open if specific reason to do so,
such as using temporary tables. Logical, default TRUE.}

\item{\code{field}}{vector with field(s) to create meta data for. Quoted string,
default NULL includes all fields.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
}
